From f6e5f329ea2291afe51257929304354ed63ee8bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allen Gregory <allengregoryiv@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:36:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Native publish always on (SPECTRUM_NATIVE_CAMERA=0 the
 only opt-out); one Java-rate flag; native pose switch is debug only

SPECTRUM_NATIVE_PUBLISH is gone: NativePublish engages per camera whenever its frames are streamed or captured natively, and verified cameras are native by default. SPECTRUM_NATIVE_PUBLISH_JAVA_FPS (30) and SPECTRUM_NATIVE_CAMERA_JAVA_FPS (5) are one flag, SPECTRUM_NATIVE_JAVA_FPS (default 5): the Java pipeline's rate while results are published natively, for the fast path and native cameras alike; SPECTRUM_STREAM_FPS (30) while a Java-fed stream is watched. SPECTRUM_NATIVE_POSE=0 documented as a debug switch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
